Local bluez patch, not upstream. Applied by scripts/install-btvirt.sh to the
`apt-get source bluez` tree AFTER bluez-4ff7deaf8c-emulator-receiving-side-
handle.patch, whose post-image it is cut against, before building
emulator/btvirt.

  tag:      adv-every-interval (the name the provenance sidecar carries)
  subject:  emulator: report a legacy advertiser every advertising interval
  cut:      2026-10-10, against bluez 5.82-1.1 (Debian) + 4ff7deaf8c, 5 hunks
  files:    emulator/btdev.c only

WHAT IT CHANGES

btvirt sends a legacy LE Advertising Report at exactly two instants: when a
scanner enables scanning (cmd_set_scan_enable_complete, one report per
advertiser that is advertising then) and when an advertiser enables
advertising (le_set_adv_enable_complete, one report per controller that is
scanning then). Between those instants the emulated air is silent. This patch
adds a timer per advertising controller, started at LE Set Advertise Enable
and stopped at disable, reset, connection or teardown, that re-sends the same
report (and the scan response, for an active scanner) to every scanning
controller once per advertising interval. The interval is the advertiser's
configured Advertising_Interval_Min (units of 0.625 ms, at least 20 ms), or
100 ms when Set Advertising Parameters was never sent. The kernel's default
is 0x0800, so a bluetoothd advertiser repeats every 1280 ms. Duplicate
filtering is not modelled, as the two enable-instant reports never modelled
it either: the host's own dedupe sees the repeats. Extended advertising
already repeats on its own timer (ext_adv_broadcast) and is untouched, as is
everything 4ff7deaf8c changes.

WHY

Real radios advertise every interval, so a scan window that overlaps one
hears the advertiser. On btvirt a scan window heard it only if it was
advertising at the instant scanning was enabled, so every test that bounds a
re-sighting measured the emulator's phase rather than the daemon. Measured
2026-10-10 (leviculum order 577): a guard test for a redial after a failed
dial was red 4 of 5 runs without btmon attached and green 5 of 5 with it,
because attaching btmon moved the instants.

THE MEASUREMENT (periculum order 590, 2026-10-10, artefacts /home/lew/ci/p590)

Two controllers on one btvirt, a bluetoothd advertiser (interval 1280 ms)
and a scanner opening three 5 s LE discovery windows, btmon on both:

  binary              window 1   window 2   window 3   (ADV_IND reports)
  4ff7deaf8c only     1          1          1          all at scan enable
  + this patch        5          5          4          1280 ms apart

On the patched binary: 577's guard test 5 of 5 green without btmon,
ble_returning_peer_resight 3 of 3 green, periculum
regression/ble_room_departure 3 of 3 green with rejoin_ms 8579, 5462, 5102.
Built binary md5 bbcd9427bf1cf23c6416de088f9b4ccb.

patch(1) ignores this header.

